WEBVTT

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.930
<i>At last, today's the day 
we'll be climbing Mt. Fuji.</i>

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.820
<i>Roughly two and a half hours 
after departing Shinjuku,</i>

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.580
<i>we will arrive at Mt. Fuji Fifth 
Station, sometime after 10 AM.</i>

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.330
Mountain Trail

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.250
Season 2 - New Climb 9

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.580
Season 2 - New Climb 9 
Nice to Meet You, Mt. Fuji!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.400
Ahh, nice and cool!

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.840
Because the Fifth Station is at 
an elevation of 2300 meters,

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.950
it's cooler than at sea level 
by about ten degrees Celsius.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:04.250
Since the height of Mt. Fuji 
is 3776 meters, that means...

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.180
halfway up would be 1888 meters.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:15.150
Mt. Fuji Fifth Station
Elevation 2305

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.660
So the Fifth Station isn't 
at the halfway point!

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:15.150
Right. The station placement seems to have 
little to do with distance or elevation.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:20.030
One opinion is that the stations were 
positioned based on the difficulty of the climb.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:34.340
Elevation
 Difference: 
~1470m

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:34.340
Rim Circuit

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.140
For example, it's a longer distance 
from the Fifth to the Sixth

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.950
than from the Sixth to the Seventh,

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.430
and the distance is even shorter 
from the Seventh to the Eighth.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:33.150
But since the path gets steeper, 
each segment is equally exhausting.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.920
It gets steeper the higher you go.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.470
L-Let's do our best!

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.290
Yeah!

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.350
Fifth Station Post Office

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.060
Fifth Station Post Office

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.060
It's a post office!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.600
Security

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.600
There's even a currency exchange!

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:54.570
Fifth Station Post Office

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.610
A bicycle?

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.570
So you can even get up here by bike...

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.230
Post Box

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.230
Look, horsies!

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.410
You can also ride up to the 
Seventh Station on horseback.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:07.830
Everyone Can Climb
Mt. Fuji Climbing

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.070
How lovely!

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:07.140
But, climbing up on your own two 
feet is more impressive, I'm sure.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:07.830
Right!

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:16.130
Celebrate: 
Mt. Fuji World 
Heritage Site

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.640
Well, shall we have lunch 
while we get acclimated?

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:16.130
Because of Mt. Fuji's high elevation, 
it's all too easy to develop altitude sickness.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.130
Altitude sickness?

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:28.640
Everyone Can Climb
Mt. Fuji Climbing

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:21.040
If you overdo it going up to high altitudes,

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.090
you may develop a headache 
and start to feel ill.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.640
For most cases, descending to the base 
of the mountain will cure it completely!

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.650
So don't overdo it, girls!

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:31.890
Okay!

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.820
Celebrate:

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.860
What'll we eat?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.820
What shall I get?

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.870
Look, they have "Eruption Curry"!

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.570
That sounds fun! I'll get that.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.130
Guess I'll have soba noodles 
with mountain vegetables.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:46.990
"Sea of Clouds Ramen"?

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.620
What kind of ramen is that?

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.620
Ramen

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.000
Since they're calling it "Sea of Clouds"...

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.110
Maybe it has wontons?

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.030
Or cooked egg?

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.220
Or grated yam?

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:56.930
Or maybe cream!

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.030
How cute!

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.040
I'll get the Sea of Clouds Ramen!

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.630
Then, I will too!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.140
Sea of Clouds Ramen

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.980
I can't wait to see what 
the Sea of Clouds is!

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.140
Right!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.640
Mt. Fuji Local Specialties

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.640
Rest House

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.640
Let's dig in!

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.770
So this is Eruption Curry!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.670
The rice must be Mt. Fuji,

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.720
so the soy-pickled vegetables are lava.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.900
That makes sense!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.360
So, how's the Sea of Clouds Ramen?

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.760
Uh, well...

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.650
It's just ordinary ramen.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:25.610
Yeah...

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.870
It was ordinary ramen, but still very tasty!

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.870
Mt. Fuji Melon Bread

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.120
Dining -
Rest Area

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:31.120
Yeah! My tummy's full!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.750
The Fifth Station's Specialty: 
Super-Popular! Mt. Fuji Melon Bread

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:37.130
Mt. Fuji Local Specialties

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:35.920
There are all kinds of souvenirs!

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.130
Look here!

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.500
Li'l Fuji

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:38.970
They're so cute!

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.500
They really are!

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.020
Nice! Maybe I'll buy one!

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.720
Buy it on the way back!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.760
Oh, true.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.860
We'd have to carry it up.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.010
Right!

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.010
Okay, it's time to head out!

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.520
Oh, just a moment.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.660
What is it?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.850
Essential Item: 
Thunderbolt Cane{kongou = vajra, Buddhist symbol of indestructible truth, also thunderbolt/Indra's weapon}
Makes a great memento!

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.850
It's a thunderbolt cane.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.930
At each mountain hut on 
the way to the summit,

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:01.480
you can stop and get a brand 
burned into the cane.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.480
World Heritage

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.900
I thought I would go collect them all!

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:09.240
I'll buy one too!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.040
If we get all the brands,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.520
it'll make a great memento!

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.750
It sure will!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.790
Prayer Tablet Hanging Spot

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.050
Let us climb to the summit safely!

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.670
Yeah, we're starting our climb now.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.380
I said I'm fine, Mom!

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.390
Okay, I'll call again later.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.890
Komitake Shrine

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.500
Onward to the summit of Mt. Fuji!

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.390
Let's go!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.040
This part is completely easy.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.800
It'll be a cinch if the 
whole climb's like this!

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.700
Like that'll happen...

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.700
Mt. Fuji Climbing Trail (Yoshida Route)

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.700
Camping Forbidden

00:05:51.700 --> 00:06:01.590
Fujimiya
Route

00:05:51.700 --> 00:06:01.590
Subashiri Route

00:05:51.700 --> 00:06:01.590
Gotenba Route

00:05:51.700 --> 00:06:01.590
Lake Yamanaka

00:05:51.700 --> 00:06:01.590
Yoshida
Route

00:05:51.700 --> 00:06:01.590
Caldera Rim

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:57.840
Mt. Fuji has multiple climbing routes, such 
as the Subashiri Route and the Gotenba Route.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:01.590
We are taking the Yoshida Route,
 the most popular one.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.050
5th Station

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.050
Ascending 
Trail

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.050
Descending
Trail

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.050
6th Station

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.050
7th Station

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.050
8th Station

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.450
Starting from the Fifth Station,

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:07.580
we'll pass the Sixth, Seventh and Eighth Stations, 
until we reach the Original Eighth Station.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:18.730
Yoshida & Subashiri Routes Summit

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:18.730
8th Station

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:18.730
9th Station

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.190
There we'll sleep in a mountain hut,

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:12.580
and then after a good rest, 
we'll head for the summit.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:14.730
Since there are many other mountain huts

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:18.070
we plan to climb at a moderate 
pace, without overdoing it.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.440
This is the Sixth Station.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:36.120
Sixth Station

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.980
Let's take a little break.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.570
Haven't we only walked for about 30 minutes?

00:06:33.570 --> 00:06:36.120
No need to rush, the mountain's 
not going anywhere!

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.620
And we've got a long way ahead of us, right?

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.130
I'll have a snack.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.460
What, already?

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:44.280
That's right!

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.920
It's important to eat before you feel hungry.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.880
You're just repeating what Kaede-san told us!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.010
What is that?

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.170
Fugashi!{stick of wheat gluten cake, usually coated in brown sugar}

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.260
Fugashi?

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.920
You're like an old man!

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.070
Wow!

00:06:58.720 --> 00:06:59.980
It's all puffed up!

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:01.610
Here, check it out!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.610
It's the difference in air pressure.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:06.480
Wow!

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.700
We're heading to the Seventh Station now.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.290
Yeah, I'm doing fine.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.400
<i>Leave partway if it gets too tough.</i>

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.890
<i>Absolutely do </i>not<i> overdo it!</i>

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:17.740
You worry too much.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:18.940
Right.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.970
Okay, I'll call again later.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:24.380
Aoi!

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.170
Time to get going!

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.130
Okay!

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.340
This path just keeps winding on and on.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.410
It's littered with rocks.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:38.860
A bulldozer!

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:43.040
That's used to transport food 
and water to the mountain huts.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.310
Maybe it'll give us a lift?

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.990
Seventh Station... reached!

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:53.570
Flower Hut

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:56.580
Fifth Station 2305m
Border Between 
Heaven & Earth
Mt. Fuji View

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.580
Flower Hut
2700m

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:58.100
That makes two so far!

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.370
Right!

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.420
Seventh Station - Sunrise Inn

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.420
Now three!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.000
Seventh Station - Sunrise Inn

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.000
You're doing quite well!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.490
There really are a lot of mountain huts.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:17.050
Tomoe Inn

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.800
Like one every ten minutes.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.480
Oh, dear!

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.410
Kaede-san?

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.060
What's wrong?

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.650
The tip of my alpenstock came off.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:27.780
Oh, no!

00:08:27.780 --> 00:08:29.150
Let's all look for it!

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.880
But this alpenstock was pretty expensive...

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:33.870
Here it is!

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:34.410
Huh?

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.430
That was quick.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:37.250
Found it!

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.090
Me too!

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:39.280
What?!

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.420
Mt. Fuji North Entrance

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.230
Aoi, you okay?

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.730
Uh? Uh-huh, just fine!

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:11.610
Let's take a little break.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:12.990
Okay...

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.030
Doing all right?

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.330
Are you cold?

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.940
I-I'm all right.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.240
You mustn't overdo it.

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.390
Don't hesitate to let us 
know if you're tired, okay?

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:32.300
Okay!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.510
<i>I can do this.</i>

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.430
Aoi!

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.830
We're heading out!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:49.480
Aoi-san?

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:50.570
I'm fine!

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.320
Just stumbled a bit.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.740
<i>Is this actually a climbing path?</i>

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:01.490
<i>It's practically a cliff.</i>

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.000
<i>The cane keeps getting in the way.</i>

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.970
That was pretty rough!

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:19.980
I know, right?

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:22.890
Yet people picture Mt. Fuji 
as a fairly easy climb.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:26.520
Toyo Inn

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:23.830
Here you go.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.290
Thank you very much.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:26.520
This makes eight!

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:29.560
It's your turn, Aoi-san.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.110
Sorry! Thanks for the reminder.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:34.610
You're right.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:37.380
Aoi-san is making some huge yawns.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:40.940
Looks like she didn't 
get much sleep last night.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:44.740
Aoi-chan, you can sleep all you want 
once we reach the mountain hut.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.120
R-Right!

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.620
The clouds have cleared away.

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:02.070
Aoi!

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.710
Look behind you!

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.280
<i>Amazing...</i>

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>The view sucks you in...</i>

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.200
You all right?

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.790
Aren't you scared?

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.660
I'm a bit scared, but fine.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:29.840
<i>I'm really glad I came!</i>

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.110
<i>I'll be fine!</i>

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.870
<i>I can do this climb.</i>

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.690
<i>Walk. Walk.</i>

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:46.300
<i>Step by step!</i>

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.260
Mountain Trail

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:59.980
To Be Continued
